  "path": "backlog/tasks/task-6.28 - Show-that-check-styles-bands-are-judged-over-100000-hands.md",
  "description": "From TASK-6.24 (decision: option B, Q-1). REQ-027's fit criterion judges each bot style's VPIP, PFR and aggression over 100,000 hands, but --check-styles gives no hint of that, so 2,000-hand runs fail for sample-noise reasons that look like tuning problems (TASK-6.24 measured 20/20 all-TAG and 12/20 Mixed 2k runs failing, none from TAG aggression: rare mixed spots used only one way, Rock VPIP 7.7\u20137.9% vs floor 8%, TAG PFR 13.7\u201313.9% vs floor 14%, Rock aggression 56.1\u201356.2% vs ceiling 55%). Update the --check-styles help line (src/playtest/cli.ts USAGE), docs/stats/style-stats.md ('In the playtest CLI') and the USAGE assertions in tests/playtest/cli.test.ts. This story's spec decides whether to also print a note when --check-styles runs with fewer than 100,000 hands. No band, bot or advice changes. Any speed or scale check goes in npm run test:slow, never in npm test or CI.",
